            "answer": "It depends on the listing. AI apps are fast and cheap but generate furniture automatically, and poorly scaled furniture is a real risk in small NYC rooms. For listings where accuracy matters, a virtual staging service where a designer composes each room in Photoshop, 3D Max and Corona is the safer choice — that is how Bella works."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging worth it?",
            "answer": "For most vacant NYC apartments, yes. Staging can't guarantee a sale, but 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search (NAR), and in New York the photos decide which showings get booked. Virtual staging furnishes them for a one-time cost per photo, with no building logistics."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging legal in New York?",
            "answer": "Yes, as long as the photos aren't misleading. Add furniture and decor only, don't hide defects or change permanent features, and clearly disclose that images are virtually staged — the NAR Code of Ethics and New York advertising rules both expect honest marketing. Every Bella order includes disclosure guidance."
          }
        },
